# E11 Predator-Prey, console version: sequential in a random order, 1 000 turns. The draws come from the seed of the
# oracle, so the C# fixes every line until the first insects leave: from then on, the C# Dictionary reuses their places
# and changes the order of the following turns, which the C++ does not reproduce (a known divergence of the library).
# Compared: the populations of the first four turns exactly, then the number of turns, populations that fit on the
# 50 x 50 grid, and the end of the simulation.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact early ^Turn ([1-4]): (\d+) doodlebugs, (\d+) ants$
fact turn ^Turn (\d+): (\d+) doodlebugs, (\d+) ants$
fact finished ^Simulation finished\.$
same early seq
same finished count
check turn count == 1000
check turn max(1) <= 2500
check turn max(2) <= 2500
